  "id": "eye-dominance",
  "term": "eye dominance",
  "definition": "Eye dominance is the tendency for one eye to be functionally preferred over the other, especially for aiming or other visual-motor tasks. It refers to preferential use rather than differences in sharpness of vision or impairment in one eye, and it can be influenced by visual experience and related biological factors.",
